{
    desc => q{u undoes visual mode character delete},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/undo_visual_delete`

Tests that **u** restores text deleted after a visual selection (**v** + motion + **d**).

**Keys:** `v`, `lll`, `d`, `u`

**initial.png**
- Buffer contains "hello world"
- Cursor at column 0 on 'h'

**after_visual_delete.png**
- Buffer contains "o world" (first 4 chars "hell" visually selected and deleted)
- Cursor at column 0 on 'o'
- Intermediate snapshot showing the deletion

**after_undo.png**
- Buffer restored to "hello world" (identical to initial)
- Visual delete fully undone
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('v');
        $ctx->keys('lll');
        $ctx->keys('d');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_visual_delete');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_undo');
    },
}
__DATA__
hello world
